WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.230
You've met acids as substances that
give away hydrogen ions: protons.

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.630
Aluminium chloride contains
no hydrogen at all.

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.430
Not a single atom.

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.010
Yet chemists still call it an acid.

5
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.410
Aluminium chloride contains
no hydrogen at all.

6
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.390
So how can it be an acid?

7
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.510
In this mission, you'll meet a
wider definition of acids and bases,

8
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.810
and see how it links
nucleophiles and electrophiles.

9
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.330
You'll draw coordination bonds,

10
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.250
and build complex ions with
the right overall charge.

11
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.870
Your mission: explain how a compound
with no hydrogen can be an acid.
